{
  "id": "ep359",
  "duration": 31.503,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "Galileo thought Saturn was three planets stuck together.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn HST 2004-03-22.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA and E. Karkoschka (University of Arizona)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_HST_2004-03-22.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.233,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.24,
      "end": 6.26,
      "text": "He looked through his telescope and saw two massive ears.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Justus Sustermans - Portrait of Galileo Galilei, 1636.jpg",
        "credit": "Justus Sustermans",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Justus_Sustermans_-_Portrait_of_Galileo_Galilei,_1636.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.233,
          "end": 4.867,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 4.867,
          "end": 6.267,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 6.26,
      "end": 9.9,
      "text": "Scientists spent decades arguing over these weird, clinging side-moons.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "The elements of astronomy; a textbook (1919) (14782253045).jpg",
        "credit": "Internet Archive Book Images",
        "license": "No restrictions",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_elements_of_astronomy;_a_textbook_(1919)_(14782253045).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 6.267,
          "end": 8.067,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 8.067,
          "end": 9.9,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.9,
      "end": 13.1,
      "text": "Then, those mysterious moons simply vanished from the sky.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Edge-On View of Saturn's Rings (1996-16-415).jpg",
        "credit": "Credit: Erich Karkoschka (University of Arizona Lunar & Planetary Lab) and NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Edge-On_View_of_Saturn%27s_Rings_(1996-16-415).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.9,
          "end": 11.433,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 11.433,
          "end": 13.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 13.1,
      "end": 15.5,
      "text": "Astronomers feared their own telescopes were failing them.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Emblemata 1624.jpg",
        "credit": "Adriaen van de Venne",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblemata_1624.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 13.1,
          "end": 15.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 15.5,
      "end": 19.42,
      "text": "Dutch astronomer Christiaan Huygens finally cracked the code in 1659.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Christiaan Huygens (Hugenius). Line engraving by F. Ottens. Wellcome M0012033.jpg",
        "credit": "Unknown author",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Christiaan_Huygens_(Hugenius)._Line_engraving_by_F._Ottens._Wellcome_M0012033.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 15.5,
          "end": 17.7,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 19.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.42,
      "end": 22.54,
      "text": "He realized the ears weren't moons or solid arms at all.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Huygens Systema Saturnium.jpg",
        "credit": "Christiaan Huygens",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Huygens_Systema_Saturnium.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.433,
          "end": 22.533,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 22.54,
      "end": 25.78,
      "text": "Saturn was actually wearing a giant, flat, floating ring.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "PIA00024 Saturn With Tethys and Dione.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PIA00024_Saturn_With_Tethys_and_Dione.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 22.533,
          "end": 24.133,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 24.133,
          "end": 25.767,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.78,
      "end": 28.36,
      "text": "This was the first time anyone discovered a ringed planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn - HST 2019-06-20.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA, A. Simon (Goddard Space Flight Center), M.H. Wong (UC Berkeley), OPAL Team",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_-_HST_2019-06-20.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.767,
          "end": 28.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.36,
      "end": 31.153,
      "text": "It looked nothing like the three planets stuck together.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn HST 2004-03-22.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA, ESA and E. Karkoschka (University of Arizona)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_HST_2004-03-22.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.367,
          "end": 31.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
